<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikola Altomanović</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1348–after 1373</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikola Altomanović was a Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> who built the largest lordship in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> as the empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> broke up. By about 1371 he held lands from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudnik">Rudnik</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzice">Užice</a> to the borders of Ragusa. In 1373 Prince Lazar and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tvrtko-i-of-bosnia">Tvrtko I of Bosnia</a> defeated him, divided his lands and had him blinded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikola-altomanovic.jpg" alt="Nikola Altomanović" width="320" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WikiNameBaks · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vojinovic_small_COA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
